      "id": 1,
      "text": "Elon began in 1881 as a North Carolina Railroad depot called Mill Point, envisioned as a shipping hub for nearby cotton mills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elon%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the Hebrew word for oak, chosen because the area was full of large oak trees when Elon College was founded.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elon%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Elon College, founded in 1889 as Graham Normal College, moved to a heavily wooded campus that still boasts those original oak trees.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elon%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Elon University, now a prominent research institution, grew from that college and remains a central landmark in the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elon%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Elon is part of the Burlington metropolitan area, linking it culturally and economically to the larger regional community.",
